  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID&#x2019;s Nagorik Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Bangladesh):  The purpose of the Elections activity is to enhance multi-party engagement and promote non-violent electoral participation. With FY 2022 funds, this new activity will conduct national surveys to understand voter priorities and attitudes toward the election, increase civic participation and freedom of speech by training journalists and civil society partners on electoral rules, and countering election-related hate speech. The activity will also hold scenario planning and lead the election assessment and observation missions (contingent on political openness and the level of open political competition ahead of the election); conduct voter education and promote voter mobilization; and promote nonviolence within student and youth wings of the political parties and create community leaders for nonviolence.  The Elections activity will directly support CDCS development objective (DO) 1 &apos;Improved Democratic Systems that Promote Transparency, Accountability, and Integrity&apos; and IR 1.3 &apos;Improved Political Processes to Prevent Further Backsliding into Authoritarianism&apos; of the CDCS (2020-2025). It will also contribute to the Department of State-USAID&apos;s Joint Strategic Plan which supports the second Integrated Country Strategy Mission Goal: &apos;Bangladesh is committed to democracy, transparency, pluralism, tolerance, good governance, and respect for human rights;&apos; and, Mission Objective 2.1 &apos;Bangladesh holds free, fair, credible, and inclusive elections, protects vulnerable populations, and ensures civil liberties.&apos; This activity will contribute towards meeting &quot;Freedom of Expression&quot; (6.3m) earmark.</narrative>
  </description>
